Package: datagrade
Type: Package
Title: Data Quality Assessment on the 'ISO/IEC' 25012 Model
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Omer Haluk", "Demirhan", email = "hlk01dn@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A single-call data quality assessment scoring a data set on the
    five inherent characteristics of the 'ISO/IEC' 25012 data quality model,
    accuracy, completeness, consistency, credibility and currentness, through
    the fifteen quality properties beneath them. Each property is measured as a
    ratio of counted data items, the form 'ISO/IEC' 25024 measurement functions
    take. Six properties are computable from a table alone; the rest compare the
    data against expectations declared through a specification object, and are
    reported as not applicable rather than approximated when none is supplied.
    Also reports missing-data patterns, duplicates, redundant columns, outliers,
    multicollinearity and distributional deviations, and returns a structured
    object with plots rather than console text alone. The statistics implement
    the methodology of the author's MSc dissertation, "Assessing Data Quality
    Management Issues in Open-Sourced Data Sets with Statistical Methodology"
    (University of Greenwich, 2024).
